    files['skills/create-prd/feature-template.md'] = '# PRD: {Feature Name}\n\n- **PRD ID:** {PRD_ID}\n- **Status:** Draft | CEO-Approved | In Progress | Completed\n- **Owner:** Manager AI (Tier 1) & Staff Agents (Tier 2)\n\n## 1. User Goal & Acceptance Criteria (`目標與驗收標準`)\n- **Goal:** {Describe the exact end-to-end outcome the user needs}\n- **Acceptance Criteria:**\n  - [ ] {Concrete, verifiable user-facing requirement 1}\n  - [ ] {Concrete, verifiable user-facing requirement 2}\n\n## 2. Scope, Architecture & Safety Constraints (`範圍與安全限制`)\n- **Files / Modules Affected:** `{list paths}`\n- **Protected Data Guard:** Never modify or delete `data/**`, `backups/**`, `migrations/**`, `*.db`, `*.sqlite*`, `*.sql`, `.env*`.\n- **Gatekeeper Approval:** Required before executing major changes or writing persistent memory.\n\n## 3. Implementation Phases (`實作階段`)\n### Phase 1: Foundation & Core Logic\n- [ ] {task 1}\n- [ ] {task 2}\n\n### Phase 2: Integration & Edge Cases\n- [ ] {task 3}\n\n## 4. Mandatory Automated Testing Plan (`強制自動化測試計畫`)\n- [ ] Unit tests covering core logic & edge cases (`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v`)\n- [ ] Integration / smoke test verifying the feature works end-to-end\n- [ ] Code quality & security checks (`ruff check .`, `mypy`, `bandit`)\n\n## 5. Definition of Done (`完成定義`)\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria implemented end-to-end (no `TODO` stubs left behind)\n- [ ] All automated tests pass 100% with verifiable output\n- [ ] Docs, configs, and agent instruction files updated cleanly\n'
    files['skills/create-prd/SKILL.md'] = '---\nname: create-prd\ndescription: Generate a structured Product Requirements Document (PRD) in docs/PRDs/active/ using feature-template.md.\n---\n# Create PRD (`create-prd`)\n\n## When to Use\n- Before implementing any new feature, major refactor, or multi-step module.\n\n## Procedure\n1. Read `skills/create-prd/feature-template.md` as the mandatory structural blueprint.\n2. Clarify scope, constraints, and non-goals with the CEO (User) before drafting.\n3. Save the completed PRD to `docs/PRDs/active/<feature-slug>.md`.\n4. Include:\n   - Problem statement & user value\n   - Functional & non-functional requirements\n   - Security / Zero-Pollution constraints (`config/safety_policy.yaml`)\n   - Acceptance criteria & verification commands\n5. Request explicit CEO approval before handing off to `ManagerAI` or `Coder`.\n'
    files['skills/phase-prd/SKILL.md'] = '---\nname: phase-prd\ndescription: Break a large PRD into sequential, independently verifiable implementation phases in docs/PRDs/active/phases/.\n---\n# Phase PRD (`phase-prd`)\n\n## When to Use\n- When a feature PRD spans more than 3 modules or requires staged rollout.\n\n## Procedure\n1. Read the parent PRD from `docs/PRDs/active/<feature>.md`.\n2. Split work into 2–5 small phases where each phase leaves tests passing.\n3. Write phase plans under `docs/PRDs/active/phases/<feature>-phase-<N>.md`.\n4. For each phase define: inputs, files touched, rollback plan, and exact verification test command.\n5. Never start Phase N+1 until Phase N passes quality gate & security review.\n'
    files['skills/language-communication/SKILL.md'] = "---\nname: language-communication\ndescription: Enforce the user's mandatory Burmese primary + Traditional Chinese (TOCFL B1) academic terminology + basic English style.\n---\n# Language & Communication Profile (`language-communication`)\n\n- Always respond primarily in natural, easy-to-read **Burmese (`မြန်မာစာ`)**.\n- Pair CS, Math, and academic concepts with **Traditional Chinese (`繁體中文`, TOCFL B1)**.\n- Explain English coding keywords in Burmese rather than assuming advanced English fluency.\n- Keep responses concise, structured with Markdown tables/bullets, and link referenced files clearly.\n"
    files['skills/prompt-refinement/SKILL.md'] = '---\nname: prompt-refinement\ndescription: Refine raw CEO requests into tamper-evident StructuredContextPayload directives with clear constraints and HITL approval.\n---\n# Prompt Refinement (`prompt-refinement`)\n\n## Procedure\n1. Read raw CEO intent and recall relevant prior episodes via `memory_read`.\n2. Rewrite vague goals into a specific, verifiable `approved_directive`.\n3. Attach mandatory safety constraints (e.g., no production schema changes, no protected data edits).\n4. Present Intent, Directive, and Constraints to the CEO for explicit approval (`y` / `n` / `e`).\n5. Never forward an unapproved or tampered payload to `ManagerAI`.\n'
    files['skills/dynamic-planning/SKILL.md'] = '---\nname: dynamic-planning\ndescription: Maintain a live, gated execution plan with Circuit Breaker (max 2 retries per step) and CEO escalation.\n---\n# Dynamic Planning (`dynamic-planning`)\n\n## Core Rules\n- Every multi-step task MUST start with a clear ordered checklist (Step 1..N) with an assigned owner (`researcher`, `coder`, `reviewer`, `security_auditor`, `devops`, `writer_tutor`).\n- Update step status immediately: `pending` -> `in_progress` -> `completed` or `failed`.\n- **Circuit Breaker (`斷路器`):** Maximum **2 retries** per step. Include concrete failure feedback on each retry.\n- **Escalation:** If a step still fails after retries, STOP downstream steps immediately and escalate to the CEO with evidence and options.\n- Always recall prior workspace memory before planning and consolidate CEO-approved results upon completion.\n'
    files['skills/quality-gate-review/SKILL.md'] = '---\nname: quality-gate-review\ndescription: Perform AST security checks, diff audits, protected-path verification, and test validation before completion.\n---\n# Quality Gate Review (`quality-gate-review`)\n\n## Checklist (Mandatory Before Done)\n1. **Security & AST Audit:** Block `eval`, `exec`, `compile`, `__import__`, unsafe `subprocess`, arbitrary file writes, and destructive SQL/shell (`DROP TABLE`, `rm -rf`).\n2. **Path Containment & Zero-Pollution:** Verify no edits touch protected patterns in `config/safety_policy.yaml` (`data/**`, `backups/**`, `migrations/**`, `*.db`, `.env*`).\n3. **Secret Redaction:** Confirm no API keys, tokens, or credentials appear in code, diffs, or logs.\n4. **Minimal Diff:** Ensure changes stay focused on the approved directive without unintended regressions.\n5. **Verification:** Run `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` (or project test suite) and confirm 100% pass.\n'
    files['skills/research-and-log-analysis/SKILL.md'] = '---\nname: research-and-log-analysis\ndescription: Investigate errors, inspect logs safely within allowed_root, and perform hybrid RAG / web research with evidence.\n---\n# Research & Log Analysis (`research-and-log-analysis`)\n\n## Procedure\n1. **Evidence First:** Inspect logs using path-contained `log_reader` (never read outside `allowed_root`).\n2. **Local Knowledge:** Query local docs with `hybrid_rag` (keyword + cosine semantic similarity) and recall past incidents via `memory_read`.\n3. **External Lookup:** Use `web_search` (Tavily / Brave / DuckDuckGo) when official docs or external error codes are needed.\n4. **Output Format:** Return structured root-cause findings containing:\n   - Exact file/log lines observed\n   - Root cause hypothesis\n   - Recommended minimal fix & risks\n'
    files['skills/bilingual-cs-tutoring/SKILL.md'] = '---\nname: bilingual-cs-tutoring\ndescription: Explain Computer Science, Math, and Engineering concepts simply in Burmese paired with Traditional Chinese (TOCFL B1) terms.\n---\n# Bilingual CS & Math Tutoring (`bilingual-cs-tutoring`)\n\n## Language Rules\n- **Primary Explanation:** Clear, simple Burmese (`မြန်မာစာ`).\n- **Academic / CS Terms:** Pair with Traditional Chinese (`繁體中文`, TOCFL B1), e.g., Algorithm (`演算法`), Matrix (`矩陣`), Derivative (`導數`), Vector Database (`向量資料庫`), Concurrency (`並行處理`).\n- **English Keywords:** Keep English basic and always explain coding/tech terms in Burmese.\n\n## Teaching Pattern\n1. Give a 1–2 sentence everyday intuition in Burmese.\n2. Show the formal term in English + Traditional Chinese (`繁體中文`).\n3. Provide a tiny runnable Python example or step-by-step trace.\n4. End with 1 quick check-for-understanding question if the user is studying.\n'
    files['.github/workflows/ci.yml'] = 'name: Personal AI Workforce CI\non: [push, pull_request]\njobs:\n  quality-and-tests:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n        with:\n          python-version: "3.12"\n      - run: pip install ruff mypy bandit\n      - run: ruff check .\n      - run: mypy agents/ api/ harness/ llm/ tools/ launcher.py demo.py main.py\n      - run: bandit -r agents/ api/ harness/ llm/ tools/ launcher.py\n      - run: python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v\n      - run: bash tests/integration/docker_sandbox_test.sh\n'
    files['tests/integration/docker_sandbox_test.sh'] = '#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\ncommand -v docker >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "Docker not installed — skipping."; exit 0; }\ndocker run --rm --network=none --read-only --cap-drop=ALL   --tmpfs /tmp:size=16m,noexec,nosuid,nodev   --memory=128m --cpus=0.5 --pids-limit=64   --security-opt=no-new-privileges --user 65534:65534   python:3.12-slim python -c "print(\'DOCKER_SANDBOX_OK\')"\n'
    files['scripts/install_recommended_skills.sh'] = '#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# AI-Driven skills.sh Skill Recommender & Installer\n# Analyzes the current project (or --workspace <path>) + 3 Workforce Reference Docs,\n# decides which skills.sh packages are needed, and installs them with user confirmation.\n#\n# Usage:\n#   bash scripts/install_recommended_skills.sh --dry-run\n#   bash scripts/install_recommended_skills.sh --workspace /path/to/MyApp --goal "FastAPI app"\n#   bash scripts/install_recommended_skills.sh --yes\n\nSCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"\nWORKFORCE_ROOT="$(cd "${SCRIPT_DIR}/.." && pwd)"\n\nexec python3 "${WORKFORCE_ROOT}/main.py" --recommend-skills "$@"\n'
